rds, $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}D}$ is measured in \"euros per dollar\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fa5bdf9-4b27-5565-9ee1-ecb9f9db4791" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Units of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edec9b0f-e74f-5f71-8e01-c49ef9dcd993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402986} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4c614-ec2d-5d40-969c-a53c3dd207e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402987} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec8af8b-c1c2-588d-b21b-584e7bda5fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Minutes per degrees Fahrenheit" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402988} {:answer/id #uuid "c8dada28-2d89-5b17-8652-6cc73bf5852f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402989} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc2b148-ac18-514b-b0ae-11c7d6164436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit squared per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edec9b0f-e74f-5f71-8e01-c49ef9dcd993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402986} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad3df16f-9c93-57df-88a3-0c0fe3164587" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "453a4f9f-dc2c-5ef4-9ab6-f86f7acd693b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48611" :question/problem "A cup of coffee sitting on a teacher's desk $t$ minutes after it has been made has the temperature $F(t)$ degrees Fahrenheit. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the temperature $F(t)$ is measured in degrees Fahrenheit and the time is measured in minutes. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t): & \\text{degrees Fahrenheit} \\\\ t: & \\text{minutes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}$ measures a change in $F(t)$ over a change in $t.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{degrees Fahrenheit}}{\\text{minutes}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}$ is measured in \"degrees Fahrenheit per minute\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fa5bdf9-4b27-5565-9ee1-ecb9f9db4791" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Units of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02ce4fcc-ff39-5197-9f0d-c4dcc3ae0157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "squared centimeters per ticket" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517172} {:answer/id #uuid "40e9d033-8470-5eda-a2c8-41ecc0879760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "tickets per squared centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517189} {:answer/id #uuid "448a766b-2d9d-58e4-9c3d-2823ad317e5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "centimeters per ticket" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517192} {:answer/id #uuid "86b21360-61a2-5321-a57d-ed31973ae8e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "squared centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517204} {:answer/id #uuid "e68d4cdc-f210-541b-b35f-12947735623e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "tickets" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02ce4fcc-ff39-5197-9f0d-c4dcc3ae0157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "squared centimeters per ticket" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517172} :answer-field/id #uuid "31e89438-e95a-5dac-9805-39b97477ac87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} 