:question/id #uuid "b76a707c-559e-596a-94b2-80c91183a360" :question/problem "A farmer estimates that she can sell $w(p)$ metric kilograms of crops at a price of $p$ dollars per kilogram. What are the units of $\\frac{dw}{dp}$?" :question/worked-solution "We have that $w(p)$ is measured in kilograms and $p$ is measured in dollars per kilogram. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w(p): & \\text{kilograms} \\\\ p: & \\text{dollars per kilogram}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}w}{\\text{d}p}$ measures a change in $w(p)$ over a change in $p.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}w}{\\text{d}p}: & \\frac{\\text{kilograms}}{\\text{dollars per kilogram}}=\\frac{\\text{squared kilograms}}{\\text{dollars}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{\\text{d}w}{\\text{d}p}$ is measured in \"squared kilograms per dollar\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fa5bdf9-4b27-5565-9ee1-ecb9f9db4791" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Units of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b1a533-c656-5613-aa27-6f4b81af8b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "euro per kilogram squared" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517171} {:answer/id #uuid "76a89f1a-68b4-56f6-a7b5-6976f4c86929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "euros" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517200} {:answer/id #uuid "9c73a8d7-71e0-51de-8a28-c32a7835f9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "euro per kilogram" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517207} {:answer/id #uuid "ecfde473-fee2-5b77-b965-8624eb7933af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517237} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f69e7c-947f-5344-a49c-fc43332e3dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "squared kilograms per euro" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4f69e7c-947f-534